I can help you get organized. Below is a focused, practical list of questions to ask Amy Foster plus a document/evidence checklist and a short action plan so you can be ready for the next steps. I’m not a lawyer — this is to help you prepare for an informed conversation with your attorney.

Clarify up front (ask Amy)
- Which specific matters are we preparing for at the next court date? (You mentioned landlord-tenant eviction, immigration court, and a custody dispute — confirm which issues are being—or will be—handled at the upcoming hearing.)
- What exactly is the relief each party is seeking and who has the burden of proof on each element?
- Is the next date a merits hearing, status conference, pretrial, or scheduling hearing?

Evidence & discovery questions to ask Amy
- After discovery closed, what gaps do you see in the evidence? What specific elements of the case do we still need to prove or rebut?
- Which documents or categories of evidence are most important for the upcoming hearing?
- Do you recommend any follow-up discovery (subpoenas, records requests, depositions)? If so, what should we subpoena and from whom?
- Are there witnesses we should plan to call? Should we take any witness declarations or affidavits now?
- Do we need expert testimony or reports (e.g., property condition expert, repair estimates, medical expert, immigration country conditions expert, forensic accountant)? If so, what deadlines apply for expert disclosure?
- Are there authentication or chain-of-custody issues for any of our documents or physical evidence (photos, videos, repairs receipts)? How should those be handled or documented?
- Are any documents that might be hearsay? If so, how can we fit them within an exception or otherwise make them admissible?
- Are translations or certified copies needed for any foreign-language documents, and who should do the translation/certification?
- Do you expect the opposing party to file any motions (e.g., in limine, summary judgment, motions to exclude evidence) that we should prepare to respond to?

Case-specific documentary checklist to confirm/collect
(Ask Amy which items from this list apply in your case)
- Lease or rental agreement; notices (pay or quit, termination, cure notices), eviction notices
- Rent ledgers, payment records (bank statements, cancelled checks, money order receipts)
- Communications: emails, text messages, written notices, repair requests, and landlord/tenant correspondence (organize chronologically)
- Photographs and videos showing property condition, dates/time stamps, originals and backups
- Repair invoices, estimates, receipts, contracts with contractors, work orders
- Inspection reports, municipal code violations, building/health department records
- Move-in/move-out condition reports and security deposit receipts
- Police reports, incident reports, or 911 records if any
- Affidavits or signed witness statements (neighbors, contractors, property managers)
- Identity, immigration, and custody-related documents if the immigration/custody matters intersect (passports, A-files, birth certificates, custody orders, child’s school/medical records)
- Any prior court orders, judgments, pleadings, motions, transcripts from earlier hearings
- Medical records or records of impact (if health or habitability is at issue)
- Financial records showing hardship or damages (pay stubs, tax returns)

Procedural & tactical questions
- What is the estimated timeline to hearing? Are there deadlines we must meet (exhibit lists, witness lists, pretrial statements)?
- Do we need to exchange exhibit/witness lists with opposing counsel and by when?
- Should we file any pre-hearing motions (e.g., motion to exclude evidence, motion in limine, motion for protective order)?
- What standard of proof will the court apply here and what does the judge expect to see in the record?
- Are there local rules for Maricopa County or for immigration court procedures we must follow (filing format, exhibit labeling, how many copies, deadlines)?
- Do you recommend mediating or negotiating a settlement before the hearing?
- If a witness is not cooperative, what are our options for obtaining testimony (subpoena, deposition, proffer)?

Witness preparation & trial logistics
- Which witnesses will the attorney call vs. helpful witness statements or affidavits?
- How should witnesses prepare? (Key topics, documents to bring, timeline for meeting with them)
- What courtroom materials do you need me to prepare (exhibit binders, exhibit lists, demonstratives)?
- Are there any special courtroom requirements (copy counts, evidence labels, technology for video/photo playback)?

Immigration/custody crossover issues (if applicable)
- If immigration consequences are relevant, ask how any eviction/custody outcome might affect immigration proceedings and whether immigration-specific evidence or country condition documents are needed.
- If custody issues overlap, ask which custody documents the immigration court (or eviction court) will consider relevant and how to protect sensitive child-related records.

Practical items to ask Amy to confirm/get for you
- Please list the top 5 documents you want me to prioritize obtaining now.
- Do you need originals, certified copies, or will photocopies suffice?
- Who should I contact to get missing documents (names, phone/email if Amy expects you to do that)?
- Are there recommended services for certified translations or obtaining certified records in Maricopa County?

Action plan you can follow now
1. Pull together a master file (digital + physical) of all documents you already have, organized by category and date.
2. Create a short gap list (what you don’t have from the checklist above).
3. Send Amy the gap list and ask which items to prioritize and whether she will issue subpoenas or wants you to obtain them.
4. Draft short witness statements (time/date/location, what they saw/know) and share with Amy for review.
5. Ask Amy for a meeting to go over strategy and expected timeline before the next court date.

Would you like me to:
- Turn these into a concise email to Amy Foster asking these questions and listing the documents you already have? (I can draft it for you.)
- Or help you build the master document checklist and a template gap list you can bring to your meeting?

If you want the draft email or a one-page checklist/gap list, tell me which documents you already have and I’ll draft it.

