2. Evidence needs & document checklist
- Do we have everything the court will likely want to see for our theory of the case? If not, what’s missing?
- Which of the following documents should I collect or update (ask Amy which apply):
  - Lease/rental agreement, addenda, move‑in/move‑out checklist
  - Rent ledgers, receipts, bank statements showing payments or nonpayment
  - Written notices (e.g., cure or quit, termination, notices to vacate)
  - Repair/maintenance requests and responses (emails, texts, written requests)
  - Photographs and videos (date/time metadata preserved), inspection reports
  - Police reports, incident reports, 911 calls
  - Correspondence (emails, texts, messenger, social media) with opposing party or tenants
  - Witness contact info and short statements (neighbors, property managers)
  - Any prior court orders, case files, eviction history
  - For immigration: copies of immigration filings, receipts, notices, passports, ID, and any case numbers
  - For custody: custody orders, visitation schedules, child records, school records, medical records (if relevant)
