How to prepare and present evidence
- Organize chronologically and label each document as an exhibit (Exhibit 1, Exhibit 2, etc.).
- Create a short exhibit list (number, title, brief description, date).
- Provide your attorney with originals (or certified copies) and multiple photocopies as requested.
- For digital evidence (texts, voicemails, emails): take screenshots with timestamps, include metadata if possible, and get witness declarations confirming authenticity.
- For recordings: check legal consent rules with your attorney (Arizona is one-party consent for recordings, but admissibility has other considerations).
- Get witness declarations or sworn affidavits now while memories are fresh — include date, time, and concise facts they observed.

